WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.794
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:02.829 --> 00:00:03.837
Sammy.

00:00:04.296 --> 00:00:06.173
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can.

00:00:06.208 --> 00:00:07.055
Go!

00:00:09.885 --> 00:00:12.095
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:14.406
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:17.476 --> 00:00:18.650
This is dad's book.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.771
I think dad wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:20.806 --> 00:00:22.814
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:22.849 --> 00:00:24.399
The family business.

00:00:24.566 --> 00:00:25.866
I got to find dad.

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:28.153
That's the only thing I can think about.

00:01:56.341 --> 00:01:57.724
I know you're just doing your job

00:01:57.759 --> 00:02:00.073
But the police have
been here a week already.

00:02:00.108 --> 00:02:02.353
I don't see why we have
to go through this again.

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:05.350
The more he tells the story
the more he believes it's true.

00:02:05.385 --> 00:02:06.809
Mrs. McKay.

00:02:08.597 --> 00:02:10.403
We know you spoke with
the local authorities.

00:02:10.538 --> 00:02:14.337
But this seems like a matter
for the State Police. So...

00:02:14.372 --> 00:02:17.003
Don't worry about how
crazy it sounds Evan.

00:02:17.038 --> 00:02:19.130
You just tell us what you saw.

00:02:19.165 --> 00:02:21.295
I was up late...

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:23.391
Watching TV.

00:02:23.426 --> 00:02:25.178
When I heard this...

00:02:25.213 --> 00:02:26.978
Weird noise.

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:30.078
What did it sound like?

00:02:30.113 --> 00:02:33.144
It sounded like a monster.

00:02:34.604 --> 00:02:37.815
Tell the officers what
you were watching on TV.

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.525
Um...

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:43.035
Godzilla versus Mothra.

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:45.093
That's my favorite Godzilla movie.

00:02:45.128 --> 00:02:47.081
So much better than the original?

00:02:47.116 --> 00:02:47.900
Totally.

00:02:47.935 --> 00:02:50.298
Yeah, he likes the remake.

00:02:50.488 --> 00:02:51.794
Yuck.

00:02:51.829 --> 00:02:53.513
That's what I mean.

00:02:55.917 --> 00:02:57.133
Evan?

00:02:57.559 --> 00:02:59.879
Did you see what this thing was?

00:02:59.914 --> 00:03:02.253
No, but I saw it grab Mr. Jenkins.

00:03:02.288 --> 00:03:04.592
It pulled him underneath the car.

00:03:04.993 --> 00:03:06.204
Then what?

00:03:08.131 --> 00:03:10.354
It took him away.

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:13.621
I heard the monster leaving.

00:03:13.656 --> 00:03:16.527
It made this really scary sound.

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:19.398
What did it sound like, Evan?

00:03:19.956 --> 00:03:24.111
Like this whining growl.

00:03:27.016 --> 00:03:28.449
Thanks for your time.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.331
So the local police
have novel out foul play.

00:03:35.966 --> 00:03:37.798
Apparently there were signs of struggle.

00:03:38.572 --> 00:03:40.461
You know, they could be right.
Could just be a kidnapping.

00:03:41.196 --> 00:03:43.246
Maybe this isn't our kind of gig.

00:03:43.281 --> 00:03:44.765
Yeah, maybe not.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.214
Except for this.

00:03:46.249 --> 00:03:48.425
Dad marked the area, Dean.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:51.129
Possible hunting grounds
of a phantom attacker.

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:52.971
Why would he even do that?

00:03:53.006 --> 00:03:57.260
Well, he found a lot of local folk law
about a dog figure that comes out at night,

00:03:57.295 --> 00:03:59.888
Grabs people then vanishes.

00:03:59.923 --> 00:04:01.521
He found this too.

00:04:01.556 --> 00:04:06.687
This county has more missing persons per
capital than anywhere else in the state.

00:04:07.104 --> 00:04:08.078
It is weird.

00:04:08.563 --> 00:04:09.450
Yeah.

00:04:09.523 --> 00:04:12.491
Don't phantom attackers usually
snatch people from their beds?

00:04:12.526 --> 00:04:14.044
Jenkins was taken from a parking lot.

00:04:14.079 --> 00:04:15.563
Well, there are all kinds, you know.

00:04:15.564 --> 00:04:19.908
Spring Hill Jack, Spanworm Gases,
they take people anywhere, anytime.

00:04:19.943 --> 00:04:22.077
Look, Dean. I don't know if
this is our kind of gig either...

00:04:22.112 --> 00:04:25.163
Yeah, you're right. We should
ask around more tomorrow.

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:26.623
Right.

00:04:27.666 --> 00:04:30.043
I saw a motel about five miles back.

00:04:30.078 --> 00:04:31.593
Whoa, whoa, easy.

00:04:31.628 --> 00:04:33.547
Let's have another round?

00:04:33.713 --> 00:04:35.138
We should get an early start.

00:04:35.173 --> 00:04:38.343
Now, you really know how to
have fun, don't you Grandma?

00:04:40.261 --> 00:04:41.375
You're right.

00:04:42.463 --> 00:04:44.444
I'll meet you outside.
I'm gonna take a leak.

00:06:32.222 --> 00:06:33.605
Hey, hey.

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:36.519
Have you guys been outside? Around
here like the last hour or so?

00:06:37.936 --> 00:06:39.104
Sam?

00:06:41.815 --> 00:06:43.176
Sammy!

00:07:02.503 --> 00:07:04.088
Sam...

00:07:15.766 --> 00:07:18.811
So, what can we do for
you Officer Washington?

00:07:18.846 --> 00:07:20.736
I'm working a missing persons.

00:07:20.771 --> 00:07:23.899
I didn't know the Jenkins case was
being covered by the State Police?

00:07:23.934 --> 00:07:26.318
Uh, no, no. It's someone else.

00:07:26.353 --> 00:07:28.035
Actually it's my cousin.

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:31.198
We were having a few laughs at
this bar down by the highway.

00:07:31.233 --> 00:07:33.081
And I haven't seen him since.

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:36.060
Did your cousin have a drinking problem?

00:07:36.095 --> 00:07:38.661
Sam? Two beers and he's doing Karaoke.

00:07:38.903 --> 00:07:41.833
No, he wasn't drunk. He was taken.

00:07:43.794 --> 00:07:45.712
All right. What's his name?

00:07:45.747 --> 00:07:47.214
Winchester.

00:07:48.465 --> 00:07:49.966
Sam Winchester.

00:07:50.508 --> 00:07:51.694
Like the riffle?

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:53.387
Like the riffle.

00:07:53.512 --> 00:07:55.103
Winchester, Sam

00:08:00.018 --> 00:08:01.985
Samuel Winchester.

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:07.651
So you know that his brother
Dean Winchester died in St. Louis.

00:08:07.818 --> 00:08:10.654
And it was excepted a murder.

00:08:11.251 --> 00:08:12.906
Yeah, Dean.

00:08:13.508 --> 00:08:15.701
Kind of the black sheep of the family.

00:08:15.736 --> 00:08:17.232
Handsome though.

00:08:22.259 --> 00:08:24.042
Well, he's not showing up
at any current field reports.

00:08:24.077 --> 00:08:26.155
I already have a lead.

00:08:26.816 --> 00:08:29.047
I saw surveillance
camera above the highway.

00:08:29.082 --> 00:08:30.582
County traffic cam.

00:08:30.617 --> 00:08:31.774
Right, yeah.

00:08:31.809 --> 00:08:33.427
I'm thinking the camera
picked up whatever took him.

00:08:33.462 --> 00:08:35.470
Oh, whoever.

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:38.890
Well, I have access to
the traffic cam footage

00:08:38.925 --> 00:08:41.723
Down at the county
works department, but...

00:08:41.758 --> 00:08:44.521
Well... Let me tell
you this the right way.

00:08:44.556 --> 00:08:48.442
Won't you fill out...

00:08:49.178 --> 00:08:50.993
A missing persons report.

00:08:54.102 --> 00:08:55.949
And sit tight over here.

00:08:56.805 --> 00:08:58.243
Officer, look uh...

00:08:59.432 --> 00:09:00.516
He's family.

00:09:01.156 --> 00:09:02.170
And I kind of...

00:09:03.134 --> 00:09:04.131
Look out for the kid.

00:09:05.074 --> 00:09:06.439
You got to let me go with you.

00:09:06.944 --> 00:09:08.411
I'm sorry, I can't do that.

00:09:10.221 --> 00:09:11.729
Well, tell me something.

00:09:11.764 --> 00:09:14.642
Your county has a fair
share of missing persons.

00:09:14.677 --> 00:09:17.478
Any of them come back?

00:09:18.187 --> 00:09:21.816
Sam's my responsibility.
And he's coming back.

00:09:21.851 --> 00:09:24.151
I'm bringing him back.

00:10:10.556 --> 00:10:11.689
Greg.

00:10:11.724 --> 00:10:13.559
I think we've got something.

00:10:14.768 --> 00:10:16.979
These traffic cam take an
image every three seconds.

00:10:17.014 --> 00:10:19.279
It's part of the amber alert program.

00:10:19.314 --> 00:10:23.902
These images were all taken around
the time your cousin Sam disappeared.

00:10:24.653 --> 00:10:26.084
This really isn't what I'm looking for.

00:10:26.119 --> 00:10:26.812
Just wait, wait.

00:10:26.857 --> 00:10:28.038
Next one.

00:10:28.073 --> 00:10:31.201
This one was taken right
after Sam left the bar.

00:10:31.236 --> 00:10:33.996
Look at the back in at that thing.

00:10:34.663 --> 00:10:37.207
Now, look at the plates.

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:41.427
The plates look new. Probably stolen.

00:10:41.462 --> 00:10:45.716
So, whoever's driving that
rust bucket must be involved.

00:10:52.473 --> 00:10:53.673
Do you hear that engine?

00:10:53.708 --> 00:10:54.939
Yeah.

00:10:55.893 --> 00:10:58.812
Kind of a whining growl, isn't it?

00:10:59.229 --> 00:11:01.148
Sure.

00:11:03.525 --> 00:11:05.486
I'll be damned.

00:11:20.417 --> 00:11:22.294
You're alive?

00:11:23.128 --> 00:11:24.428
Hey, you okay?

00:11:24.463 --> 00:11:27.424
Does it look like I'm doing okay?

00:11:28.552 --> 00:11:29.655
Where are we?

00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:31.220
I don't know.

00:11:31.903 --> 00:11:33.103
Country, I think.

00:11:33.757 --> 00:11:35.328
Smells like the country.

00:11:36.002 --> 00:11:37.518
You're Jenkins, aren't you?

00:11:38.054 --> 00:11:38.977
Yeah.

00:11:40.835 --> 00:11:42.272
Wow, I was looking for you.

00:11:42.603 --> 00:11:43.400
Oh, yeah?

00:11:43.435 --> 00:11:44.197
Yeah.

00:11:44.232 --> 00:11:47.826
Well, no offense. But
this is a piss poor rescue.

00:11:47.861 --> 00:11:51.406
Well, my brother's out there right
now too. He's looking for us. So...

00:11:51.441 --> 00:11:53.551
So, he's not gonna find us.

00:11:53.586 --> 00:11:55.626
We're in the middle of nowhere.

00:11:55.661 --> 00:11:58.580
Waiting for them to come back
and do God knows what to us.

00:11:58.615 --> 00:12:00.339
What are they?

00:12:01.061 --> 00:12:01.775
Have you seen them?

00:12:02.476 --> 00:12:02.702
What are you talking about?

00:12:02.703 --> 00:12:04.586
Whatever grabbed us,
what did they look like?

00:12:04.621 --> 00:12:06.338
See for yourself.

00:12:25.482 --> 00:12:26.615
Leave me alone.

00:12:27.384 --> 00:12:29.278
Don't touch me. Leave me alone!

00:12:46.619 --> 00:12:48.788
I'll be damned.

00:12:51.624 --> 00:12:53.216
They're just people.

00:12:53.251 --> 00:12:56.504
Yeah, what did you expect?

00:12:56.921 --> 00:12:58.568
How often do they feed you?

00:12:58.603 --> 00:12:59.691
Once a day.

00:13:00.008 --> 00:13:03.511
They use that thing over
there to open the cage.

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:06.055
And that's the only time you see them?

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:08.474
So far. But I'm waiting.

00:13:08.509 --> 00:13:10.410
Waiting for what?

00:13:10.445 --> 00:13:12.276
Their baiting time, man.

00:13:12.311 --> 00:13:14.536
I think that's the least
of your worries right now.

00:13:14.571 --> 00:13:15.303
Oh, yeah?

00:13:15.338 --> 00:13:15.738
Yeah.

00:13:15.773 --> 00:13:17.028
What do you they want then?

00:13:17.685 --> 00:13:19.575
Depends on who they are.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:22.613
They're bunch of psycho
hill-Billy red neck if you ask me.

00:13:22.648 --> 00:13:25.366
Looking for love in
all the wrong places.

00:13:39.752 --> 00:13:41.973
Okay, the next traffic cam

00:13:42.008 --> 00:13:45.595
Is fifty miles from here and your
pickup didn't pass that one. So...

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:47.572
So, it must have pulled up somewhere.

00:13:48.016 --> 00:13:49.480
I don't see any other roads here.

00:13:49.911 --> 00:13:54.020
Well, a lot of these back woods
properties have their own private roads.

00:13:54.523 --> 00:13:55.855
Great.

00:14:08.723 --> 00:14:10.077
So, Gregory.

00:14:10.593 --> 00:14:11.085
Yeah.

00:14:11.887 --> 00:14:13.128
I ran your badge number.

00:14:13.163 --> 00:14:15.860
It's routine when working
A case with State Police

00:14:15.895 --> 00:14:17.752
For county purposes when we have you.

00:14:18.445 --> 00:14:21.589
And they just got back to me...

00:14:25.213 --> 00:14:27.386
Says here your badge was stolen.

00:14:28.172 --> 00:14:31.377
And there's a picture of you.

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:37.425
I lost some weight.

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:39.807
And I got that Michael
Jackson skin disease...

00:14:39.842 --> 00:14:40.585
Okay.

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:42.100
Would you step out of the car please?

00:14:42.135 --> 00:14:43.003
Look, look, look.

00:14:45.053 --> 00:14:47.222
If you want to arrest me that's fine.

00:14:47.257 --> 00:14:49.433
I'll cooperate. I swear.

00:14:49.468 --> 00:14:51.608
But first please...

00:14:51.643 --> 00:14:52.635
Let me find Sam.

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:54.192
I don't even know who you are.

00:14:54.514 --> 00:14:56.696
Or if this Sam person is missing.

00:14:56.731 --> 00:14:59.067
Look into my eyes and tell
me if I'm lying about this.

00:14:59.102 --> 00:15:02.561
Identity theft. You're
impersonating an officer.

00:15:03.607 --> 00:15:05.273
Here's the thing. When...

00:15:05.564 --> 00:15:07.416
When we were young...

00:15:07.451 --> 00:15:10.458
I pretty much pulled him from a fire.

00:15:11.496 --> 00:15:14.635
And ever since then I
felt responsible for him.

00:15:15.097 --> 00:15:18.628
You know, like it's my
job to keep him safe.

00:15:20.672 --> 00:15:24.968
I'm just afraid if we
don't find him fast.

00:15:25.927 --> 00:15:27.888
Please...

00:15:28.346 --> 00:15:31.308
He's my family.

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:34.234
I'm sorry.

00:15:34.269 --> 00:15:36.730
You've given me no choice.

00:15:36.765 --> 00:15:39.191
I have to take you in.

00:15:52.897 --> 00:15:55.838
After we find Sam Winchester.

00:15:58.543 --> 00:16:00.072
What's your name again?

00:16:00.107 --> 00:16:01.382
It's Sam.

00:16:01.946 --> 00:16:05.325
Why won't you give it up
Sammy. There's no way out.

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:06.951
Don't...

00:16:07.535 --> 00:16:09.078
Call me...

00:16:09.113 --> 00:16:10.621
Sammy.

00:16:13.082 --> 00:16:15.460
What is it?

00:16:19.464 --> 00:16:20.805
It's a bracket.

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:24.594
Well, thank God a bracket.
Now we got them, huh?

00:16:26.888 --> 00:16:29.474
Must have been a short.

00:16:32.226 --> 00:16:35.521
Maybe you knocked something loose.

00:16:38.399 --> 00:16:40.117
I think you should get
back in there Jenkins.

00:16:40.152 --> 00:16:40.711
What?

00:16:41.187 --> 00:16:42.869
This isn't right.

00:16:42.904 --> 00:16:44.885
Do you want to get out of here?

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:46.831
Yeah, but that was too easy.

00:16:46.866 --> 00:16:49.077
Look, I'm gonna get out of
here. I'm gonna send help. Okay?

00:16:49.112 --> 00:16:49.934
Okay. Don't worry.

00:16:49.969 --> 00:16:50.629
No.

00:16:50.664 --> 00:16:53.456
I'm serious, Jenkins.
This might be a trap.

00:16:53.491 --> 00:16:55.416
Bye, Sammy.

00:16:55.708 --> 00:16:57.627
Jenkins!

00:17:37.416 --> 00:17:39.376
Thank you.

00:19:12.444 --> 00:19:14.195
Okay, officer.

00:19:14.446 --> 00:19:16.021
Look I'm gonna press my luck.

00:19:16.056 --> 00:19:17.976
Your luck is so pressed.

00:19:18.276 --> 00:19:19.909
Right.

00:19:20.201 --> 00:19:22.078
I was wondering...

00:19:22.328 --> 00:19:24.726
Why are you helping me out anyway?

00:19:24.761 --> 00:19:27.125
Why don't you just lock me up?

00:19:28.042 --> 00:19:31.379
My brother Riley
disappeared three years ago.

00:19:31.414 --> 00:19:33.763
A lot like Sam.

00:19:33.798 --> 00:19:35.675
We searched for him but...

00:19:35.710 --> 00:19:37.927
Nothing.

00:19:38.595 --> 00:19:41.514
I know what it's like to
feel responsible for someone.

00:19:41.549 --> 00:19:43.850
And for them...

00:19:46.436 --> 00:19:49.006
Come on, let's keep at it.

00:19:52.567 --> 00:19:54.792
Wait, wait. Pull over here. Pull over.

00:20:06.551 --> 00:20:08.718
It's the first turn
off I've seen so far.

00:20:09.792 --> 00:20:11.544
You stay here, I'll check it out.

00:20:11.579 --> 00:20:12.680
No way.

00:20:12.715 --> 00:20:13.781
Hey...

00:20:14.464 --> 00:20:16.278
You're a civilian.

00:20:16.313 --> 00:20:18.057
And a felon, I think.

00:20:18.092 --> 00:20:20.511
I'm not taking you with me.

00:20:21.037 --> 00:20:22.388
You're not going without me.

00:20:25.624 --> 00:20:27.775
All right. You promise...

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:31.064
You won't get involved.
You let me handle it.

00:20:31.703 --> 00:20:33.041
Yeah, I promise.

00:20:33.076 --> 00:20:34.984
Shake on it.

00:20:38.911 --> 00:20:40.782
Oh, come on.

00:20:41.532 --> 00:20:43.833
This is ridiculous.

00:20:44.568 --> 00:20:46.612
Katherine, I really think
you're gonna need my help.

00:20:46.647 --> 00:20:49.990
I'll manage. Thank you.

00:20:53.452 --> 00:20:56.372
I got to start carrying paper clips.

00:21:26.985 --> 00:21:28.391
Hello?

00:21:31.615 --> 00:21:33.463
Anybody home?

00:21:48.424 --> 00:21:49.668
Hi.

00:21:51.009 --> 00:21:52.780
How are you?

00:21:58.559 --> 00:22:00.234
Who are you?

00:22:00.269 --> 00:22:04.565
I'm Katherine. I'm a deputy.

00:22:04.600 --> 00:22:06.608
What's your name?

00:22:06.643 --> 00:22:08.242
Missy.

00:22:08.277 --> 00:22:10.737
Missy? That's a pretty name.

00:22:10.772 --> 00:22:13.198
Missy, is your mom home?

00:22:13.233 --> 00:22:15.624
She's dead.

00:22:15.659 --> 00:22:19.496
I'm sorry, what about your dad?

00:22:19.788 --> 00:22:22.082
No?

00:22:23.125 --> 00:22:26.170
Can I come in for a minute?

00:22:26.587 --> 00:22:28.922
I just want you look at a picture.

00:22:28.957 --> 00:22:31.357
Have you seen that guy?

00:22:33.469 --> 00:22:35.825
Look at that picture.

00:22:37.848 --> 00:22:39.356
What?

00:22:39.391 --> 00:22:41.894
That's gonna hurt.

00:22:44.730 --> 00:22:46.363
Missy, sweetheart.

00:22:46.398 --> 00:22:48.901
Go tell your brothers,
I want to see them.

00:22:48.936 --> 00:22:51.487
Yes, daddy.

00:23:08.212 --> 00:23:10.589
Son of a bitch.

00:24:14.226 --> 00:24:16.467
But I've never seen him so angry before.

00:24:16.502 --> 00:24:19.783
Never been followed
by the police before.

00:24:34.830 --> 00:24:37.208
You all right?

00:24:40.252 --> 00:24:43.213
Are you Sam Winchester? Aren't you?

00:24:43.248 --> 00:24:45.003
Yeah.

00:24:45.038 --> 00:24:46.759
You're...

00:24:47.134 --> 00:24:50.471
You're cousin's looking for you.

00:24:51.555 --> 00:24:53.411
Thank God.

00:24:53.446 --> 00:24:55.482
Where is he?

00:24:55.517 --> 00:24:57.519
He uh...

00:24:57.853 --> 00:25:01.065
I cuffed him to my car.

00:25:22.670 --> 00:25:24.421
Sam?

00:25:25.047 --> 00:25:26.382
Are you hurt?

00:25:26.417 --> 00:25:28.133
No.

00:25:28.342 --> 00:25:30.844
Damn, it's good to see you.

00:25:31.595 --> 00:25:34.682
How did you get out of the cuffs?

00:25:34.717 --> 00:25:37.559
I know a trick or two.

00:25:38.560 --> 00:25:40.521
All right.

00:25:40.771 --> 00:25:42.231
Oh.

00:25:42.523 --> 00:25:44.865
These locks they're gonna be a bitch.

00:25:44.900 --> 00:25:48.112
Well, there's some kind of
automatic control. Right there.

00:25:48.347 --> 00:25:50.188
Have you seen them?

00:25:50.223 --> 00:25:51.488
Yeah.

00:25:51.523 --> 00:25:53.734
Dude, they're just people.

00:25:53.769 --> 00:25:55.826
And they jumped you?

00:25:55.861 --> 00:25:59.364
Must be getting a little
rusty there, kiddo.

00:25:59.399 --> 00:26:00.386
What do they want?

00:26:00.421 --> 00:26:01.150
I don't know.

00:26:01.151 --> 00:26:03.010
They let Jenkins go, but...

00:26:03.045 --> 00:26:04.835
That was some sort of trap.

00:26:04.870 --> 00:26:06.947
It doesn't make any sense to me.

00:26:06.982 --> 00:26:08.337
Oh, well that's the point.

00:26:08.372 --> 00:26:09.548
You know with...

00:26:09.583 --> 00:26:13.587
Our usual play mates there's rules,
here's patterns. But with people...

00:26:13.622 --> 00:26:15.429
They're just crazy.

00:26:15.464 --> 00:26:18.008
You see anything else out there?

00:26:18.800 --> 00:26:21.365
He has about a dozen junk cars
out back. Plates from all over.

00:26:21.400 --> 00:26:23.930
So, I'm thinking when they take
someone they take their car too.

00:26:23.965 --> 00:26:28.060
Did you see a black mustang?
Out there about ten years old?

00:26:28.095 --> 00:26:31.605
Yeah, actually I did.

00:26:33.281 --> 00:26:36.284
Your brothers?

00:26:37.494 --> 00:26:39.955
I'm sorry.

00:26:41.247 --> 00:26:44.334
Let's get you guys out of here. Then
we'll take care of those bastards.

00:26:44.369 --> 00:26:46.503
It takes a key, key?

00:26:46.538 --> 00:26:47.844
I don't know.

00:26:47.879 --> 00:26:49.756
All right, I better go find it.

00:26:49.791 --> 00:26:51.424
Hey.

00:26:51.800 --> 00:26:53.718
Be careful.

00:26:53.953 --> 00:26:55.920
Yeah.

00:28:07.325 --> 00:28:09.327
Well, I'll say it again.

00:28:09.362 --> 00:28:11.954
Demons I get.

00:28:12.121 --> 00:28:14.540
People are crazy.

00:29:04.420 --> 00:29:06.026
What the...

00:30:41.986 --> 00:30:44.656
It's okay. I'm not gonna hurt you.

00:30:44.989 --> 00:30:46.699
I know.

00:30:46.908 --> 00:30:48.201
Daddy!

00:30:48.326 --> 00:30:49.661
Daddy!

00:30:49.911 --> 00:30:51.454
Daddy!

00:30:52.080 --> 00:30:53.915
Daddy!

00:31:22.326 --> 00:31:25.413
I'm gonna kick your ass first.

00:31:25.746 --> 00:31:27.665
Then yours.

00:31:39.552 --> 00:31:41.345
Come on.

00:31:41.512 --> 00:31:42.895
Let's hunt.

00:31:42.930 --> 00:31:44.890
Yeah, this one's a fighter.

00:31:44.925 --> 00:31:47.893
Sure be fun to hunt.

00:31:48.561 --> 00:31:50.444
Oh, you got to be kidding me.

00:31:50.479 --> 00:31:52.565
This is what this is about? You...

00:31:52.600 --> 00:31:55.401
You yahoos hunt people?

00:31:56.902 --> 00:32:00.364
You ever killed before?

00:32:00.399 --> 00:32:02.366
What?

00:32:03.659 --> 00:32:06.287
Well, it depends on what you mean.

00:32:06.322 --> 00:32:09.630
I've hunted all my life.

00:32:09.665 --> 00:32:13.377
Just like my father, his before him.

00:32:13.412 --> 00:32:15.504
I've hunted deer...

00:32:15.539 --> 00:32:17.304
And bear...

00:32:17.339 --> 00:32:21.385
I even got a coo-Coo once. Oh boy.

00:32:21.802 --> 00:32:24.597
But the best hunt...

00:32:24.632 --> 00:32:27.099
Is human.

00:32:28.267 --> 00:32:31.068
Oh, there's nothing like it.

00:32:31.103 --> 00:32:35.573
Holding their life in your hands.

00:32:35.608 --> 00:32:40.529
Seeing the fear in their
eyes just before they go dark.

00:32:40.564 --> 00:32:44.450
Makes you feel powerful alive.

00:32:44.685 --> 00:32:47.403
You're a sick puppy.

00:32:48.070 --> 00:32:50.246
We give them a weapon.

00:32:50.281 --> 00:32:53.158
Give him a fighting chance.

00:32:53.393 --> 00:32:55.701
It's kind of like...

00:32:55.736 --> 00:32:58.745
Our tradition passed down

00:32:58.780 --> 00:33:04.001
Father to son, cost
only one or two a year.

00:33:04.036 --> 00:33:09.082
Never enough to bring the lot
down we've never been that sloppy.

00:33:09.117 --> 00:33:11.627
Yeah, well. Don't save yourself short.

00:33:11.662 --> 00:33:14.338
You're plenty of sloppy.

00:33:15.672 --> 00:33:19.635
So what? You're with that pretty cop?

00:33:24.932 --> 00:33:27.935
Are you a cop?

00:33:29.561 --> 00:33:32.112
If I tell you...

00:33:32.147 --> 00:33:36.026
You promise not to make
me into an ash tray?

00:33:40.288 --> 00:33:43.875
Only reason I don't let my
boys take you right here now

00:33:43.910 --> 00:33:47.385
Is that there's
something I need to know.

00:33:47.420 --> 00:33:50.206
Yeah, how about it's not
nice to marry your sister.

00:33:51.077 --> 00:33:56.763
Tell me, any of the cops
go come looking for you?

00:33:56.798 --> 00:33:58.104
Oh, eat me.

00:33:58.139 --> 00:34:01.434
No, no, no. Wait. You actually might.

00:34:03.937 --> 00:34:06.821
You think this is funny?

00:34:06.856 --> 00:34:10.777
You've brought this down on my family.

00:34:12.520 --> 00:34:14.487
All right?

00:34:14.522 --> 00:34:17.546
You want to play games?

00:34:17.581 --> 00:34:20.570
We'll play some games.

00:34:22.864 --> 00:34:27.577
Looks like we're gonna have a
hunt tonight after all, boys.

00:34:27.612 --> 00:34:30.663
And you get to pick the animal.

00:34:30.698 --> 00:34:33.037
The boy or the cop.

00:34:33.072 --> 00:34:35.376
Okay, wait, wait.

00:34:35.960 --> 00:34:38.838
Look, nobody's coming for
me. All right? It's just us.

00:34:38.873 --> 00:34:42.091
You don't choose, I will.

00:34:43.635 --> 00:34:47.055
Oh, you son of a bitch!

00:34:51.726 --> 00:34:54.402
Next time, I'll take an eye.

00:34:54.437 --> 00:34:58.233
All right, all right. The
guy. The guy. Take the guy!

00:34:58.858 --> 00:35:00.617
Lee.

00:35:00.952 --> 00:35:03.412
Go do it.

00:35:03.955 --> 00:35:06.561
Don't let him out though.

00:35:06.596 --> 00:35:09.168
Shoot him in the cage.

00:35:10.294 --> 00:35:12.338
What?

00:35:12.547 --> 00:35:14.323
I thought you said you
were gonna hunt him.

00:35:14.358 --> 00:35:15.589
You're gonna give him a chance!

00:35:15.624 --> 00:35:17.161
Lee!

00:35:17.196 --> 00:35:19.053
When you're done with the boy.

00:35:19.088 --> 00:35:22.014
Shoot the bitch too.

00:35:24.350 --> 00:35:29.814
We're cleaning this mess up before
any more cops come running out here.

00:35:38.614 --> 00:35:40.491
What are you doing?

00:35:48.624 --> 00:35:49.792
Hey!

00:35:51.836 --> 00:35:54.297
You hurt my brother,
I'll kill you. I swear.

00:35:54.332 --> 00:35:56.712
I'll kill you all.

00:35:56.747 --> 00:35:59.093
I will kill you all!

00:35:59.768 --> 00:36:01.645
Lee!

00:36:11.822 --> 00:36:13.490
Damn.

00:36:18.704 --> 00:36:20.372
Lee!

00:36:22.541 --> 00:36:25.210
Jack, you come with me.

00:36:25.245 --> 00:36:26.670
Missy.

00:36:26.879 --> 00:36:29.298
You watch him now.

00:36:38.140 --> 00:36:39.350
Lee?

00:36:39.641 --> 00:36:41.393
Where are you?

00:36:45.439 --> 00:36:46.899
Lee?

00:36:48.976 --> 00:36:51.562
Damn it. Jack, hit the lights.

00:36:52.896 --> 00:36:55.315
They must have pulled the fuses.

00:38:26.857 --> 00:38:28.558
You stupid...

00:38:29.559 --> 00:38:30.810
Hey!

00:39:06.762 --> 00:39:08.723
I'll watch this one. You go ahead.

00:39:13.402 --> 00:39:15.988
Go ahead.

00:39:26.457 --> 00:39:28.883
You hurt my family.

00:39:28.918 --> 00:39:31.441
I'm gonna bleed you bitch.

00:39:31.476 --> 00:39:33.965
You killed my brother.

00:39:34.000 --> 00:39:36.342
Your brother?

00:39:37.552 --> 00:39:39.435
Now I see.

00:39:39.470 --> 00:39:42.056
Just tell me why.

00:39:43.567 --> 00:39:46.310
Because it's fun.

00:40:09.174 --> 00:40:09.988
Where's the girl?

00:40:10.023 --> 00:40:11.391
I locked her in the closet.

00:40:11.426 --> 00:40:13.553
What about the dad?

00:40:15.180 --> 00:40:18.809
Shot. Trying to escape.

00:40:29.444 --> 00:40:32.697
I think the car's at the police station.

00:40:32.864 --> 00:40:36.159
Backup units on route to your location.

00:40:38.745 --> 00:40:40.580
So...

00:40:40.914 --> 00:40:44.209
State Police and the FBI are
gonna be here within the hour.

00:40:44.244 --> 00:40:47.128
They're gonna want to talk to you.

00:40:47.629 --> 00:40:51.925
I suggest that you're
both long gone by then.

00:40:52.092 --> 00:40:53.927
Thanks.

00:40:56.137 --> 00:40:57.910
Hey, listen. I don't
mean to press our luck.

00:40:57.945 --> 00:40:59.683
But we're kind of in
the middle of nowhere.

00:40:59.718 --> 00:41:02.060
You think we could catch a ride?

00:41:02.095 --> 00:41:04.354
Start walking.

00:41:05.438 --> 00:41:07.857
Duck if you see a SWAT car.

00:41:07.892 --> 00:41:10.277
Sounds great to me. Thanks.

00:41:10.986 --> 00:41:12.904
Listen...

00:41:14.639 --> 00:41:17.433
I'm sorry about your brother.

00:41:17.892 --> 00:41:19.894
Thank you.

00:41:21.229 --> 00:41:22.779
It was really hard not
knowing what happened to him.

00:41:22.814 --> 00:41:28.319
I thought it would be easier
once I knew the truth. But...

00:41:29.445 --> 00:41:31.864
It isn't really.

00:41:36.703 --> 00:41:39.330
Anyway you should go.

00:41:52.593 --> 00:41:55.096
Don't ever do that again.

00:41:55.131 --> 00:41:56.270
Do what?

00:41:56.305 --> 00:41:58.266
Go missing like that.

00:41:59.684 --> 00:42:01.978
You were worried about me.

00:42:02.729 --> 00:42:06.399
I'm saying, you vanish like that
again I'm not looking for you.

00:42:06.691 --> 00:42:07.711
Sure you will.

00:42:07.746 --> 00:42:08.468
I'm not.

00:42:09.318 --> 00:42:11.577
So you got saddled on by
a 13 year old girl, huh?

00:42:11.612 --> 00:42:12.598
Oh, shut up!

00:42:12.633 --> 00:42:14.570
Just saying getting rusty there, kiddo.

00:42:15.116 --> 00:42:16.784
Shut up!



